# Who reviews the documentation.
#
# GitHub auto-requests a review from these owners on any pull request touching a matching
# path. It is advisory: it blocks nothing unless "Require review from Code Owners" is
# switched on in branch protection, which it is not.
#
# This repo is the canonical wiki, so almost everything in it is documentation. The
# exceptions are listed last and deliberately have no owner:
#
#   * generated files — nobody can meaningfully review a regenerated index, and asking
#     them to is how people learn to approve docs without reading them.
#   * llmwiki/ — the rendering engine, maintained upstream and never edited here.
#
# Spec: https://tech.helloally.ai/#/wiki/contributing/docs-system.md

/wiki/                      @ajeygore @gksoriginals @sandeepmalhotragithub @shubhambhoite502
